{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789774105,"nonce":"qHR+QKGUlRc2XofDBCzQADvS8HA=","title":"the selective import merge leaves a referenced stdlib callee body-less (Int64.copy)","message":"Referencing `haxe.___Int64.toString` from Int64's `__vtable_init__` (a\n`fn_ref`, as the constructor wrappers already are) makes Cranelift's\nfinalize panic with \"can't resolve symbol copy\" on the USER module: the\nmerged copy of `haxe.Int64.divMod` calls `copy`, and both `copy` entries\nin the merged module are body-less stubs, though `haxe.Int64.copy` has a\nbody in Int64.hx's own module. `retain_referenced_stdlib_functions`\n(compilation/mod.rs) walks direct references from name roots; the import\nmerge that copies Int64 into the user module evidently does not carry the\ncallee. Reproduce: register stdlib toStrings in\n`generate_vtable_init_function` (drop the `in_stdlib` guard) and run any\nprogram. Until fixed, `Std.string` of a stdlib class instance held as\nDynamic prints the class name rather than its toString.","files":null}]}